rname>Malone</surname> <given-names>DC</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Billups</surname> <given-names>SJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Valuck</surname> <given-names>RJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Carter</surname> <given-names>BL</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Development of a chronic disease indicator score using a Veterans Affairs Medical Center medication database. IMPROVE Investigators.</article-title><source>J Clin Epidemiol</source> <year>1999</year>;<volume>52</volume>:<fpage>551</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0895-4356(99)00029-3</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10408995</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11. </label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</collab> Respiratory and enteric virus national trends. Atlanta: The Centers; <year>2007</year></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>